                <pb facs="0662" n="638" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v19/pg638"/>

                <head>158. National Security Council Report<anchor n="1" xml:id="d158-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">NSC 5724</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                ><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                                when="1957-11-07">November 7, 1957</date>.</hi></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">REPORT TO THE PRESIDENT BY THE SECURITY RESOURCES PANEL OF
                    THE ODM SCIENCE ADVISORY COMMITTEE ON DETERRENCE
                    AND SURVIVAL IN THE NUCLEAR AGE</p>
                <p>Note by the Executive Secretary to the National Security Council</p>
                <list type="references">
                    <head>REFERENCES</head>
                    <item>A. NSC 5408</item>
                    <item>B. NSC 5606</item>
                    <item>C. NSC Actions Nos. 1642, 1691, 1760, 1776
                        and 1811</item>
                    <pb facs="0663" n="639" xml:id="pg639"/>
                    <item>D. Memo for NSC from Executive Secretary,
                        subject: “Civil Defense Legislative Program for FY 1958”, dated January 3, 1957</item>
                    <item>E. NSC 5709</item>
                    <item>F. Memos for NSC from Executive Secretary,
                        subject: “A Federal Shelter Program for Civil Defense”, dated July 2 and
                        August 14, 1957</item>
                    <item>G. Report by CIA, subject: “Current
                        Appraisal of the Civil Defense Shelter Program in the USSR”, dated November 5, 1957</item>
                    <item>H. NSC Action No. 1814<anchor n="2"
                            xml:id="d158-f2"/></item>
                </list>
                <p>The enclosed Report to the President on the subject, prepared by the Security
                    Resources Panel of the ODM Science Advisory
                    Committee pursuant to NSC Action No. 1691–b–(2),
                    is transmitted herewith for consideration by the National Security Council.</p>
                <p>The National Security Council noted and discussed an oral presentation of the
                    enclosed Report at its 343rd meeting today. Further Council action on the
                    enclosed Report will be as specified in the Record of Actions of the 343rd
                    Council meeting (NSC Action No. 1814).</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">It is requested that special security precautions be
                        observed in the handling of this Report, and that access to it be limited on
                        a strict need-to-know basis.</hi></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">James S. Lay,
                                Jr</hi>.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d158-f3"
                    /></signed></closer>






